    <Program class="ca.nrcan.gc.OEE.ERS.ErsProgram">
        <Labels>
            <English>EnerGuide Rating System</English>
            <French>Système de cote ÉnerGuide</French>
        </Labels>
        <Version major="15" minor="6" build="18345">
            <Labels>
                <English>v15.6b18345</English>
                <French>v15.6b18345</French>
            </Labels>
        </Version>
        <SdkVersion major="1" minor="16" build="18345">
            <Labels>
                <English>v1.16b18345</English>
                <French>v1.16b18345</French>
            </Labels>
        </SdkVersion>
        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Air Leakage Areas:



Attic hatch should have some more weight added to it. It is not heavy enough to compress seal around hatch. Add some Rigid insulation to weigh it down.



Side Door is quite leaky. Needs weatherstripping.



Most of the windows are leaky around the window seals. Silicon may fix this.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>Add R-15 to the exterior.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on insulation upgrades and the criteria for these products.</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>Add R20-25 insulation in attic. May want to spray foam in compressed heel areas if there is not enough room.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on insulation upgrades and the criteria for these products.</ceilings>
                <windows>Upgrade windows to energy star zone 3 rated.</windows>
                <VentilationSystem>There is all the ductwork and vents for the HRV but there was no signs of it in the house. If there is one, have it balanced and serviced. If there is not one, It would be a very easy installation.



If there is air sealing upgrades completed to the home, it will make it tighter, but it will not allow for the home to breathe as it was before. A mechanical ventilation system such as a HRV/ERV should be installed to allow the home to be properly ventilated. Not installing a system after air sealing can lead to issues with mold and mildew.



A HRV/ERV could replace the humidistat as well as the HRV/ERV will recovery heated exhaust air via a heat exchanger and preheat supply air with the extracted heat, making the units very efficient. 



HRV = Heat Recovery Ventilator

ERV = Enthalpy Recovery Ventilator



ERV also can control indoor humidity levels as well.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on ventilation systems and the criteria for these products.

</VentilationSystem>
                <HotWaterSystem>Replaced Conventional tank to a instantaneous on-demand DHW unit with EF of 0.95



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on DHW and the criteria for these products.</HotWaterSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>Upgrade boiler to a condensing gas boiler with a 95% AFUE. This system will have direct supply/exhaust which will eliminate the need for the fresh supply air duct in the furnace room. This will decrease the amount of oil burned during the heating season and will reduce cold air entering the home. 



Do not removed supply air if only one of boiler or hot water is replaced as the other will still need it.



A combo condensing gas bolier/DHW combo would be recommended as well.</HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
